# What fzf-files.sh needs, declared beside it. The preview tools are shared with fzf-tags.sh,
# and they are declared here because this is the file whose preview defines what they do.
# Format is name | kind | locator | policy | reason, and the collector stamps the consumer.
#
# The preview tools are optional because a missing one only breaks the preview pane of a
# picker that otherwise works, so the pane shows a shell error rather than the picker
# refusing to open.
fd    | path | fd    | required | listing files, and finding repositories by their .git directory
bat   | path | bat   | optional | syntax highlighted file previews, the pane shows an error without it
eza   | path | eza   | optional | tree previews of a directory, the pane shows an error without it
chafa | path | chafa | optional | image previews in the terminal, the pane shows an error without it
nvim  | path | nvim  | optional | opening a chosen file, the copy action still works without it
